// mustreject retype / widen-through-let: `types.cell(stmt)` is true for every
// let whose initializer's node type is a TVar (a call's return cell, bind.rs
// keeps node.typ()), not only a let over bottom, so no retype probe is made
// here although the writer `v <- "tm"` is refused
// ("v is i64 and cannot hold string"). typemorph-one prints only
// widen-consumer probes for this body; `{ let v = 1; let w = v + 1; w }`
// gets retype probes.
{ let f = |x: i64| -> i64 x; let v = f(1); let w = v + 1; w }
